---
description: Core repository context and navigation requirements
alwaysApply: true
---

Read and follow @AGENTS.md before performing repository work.

Key boundaries:

- `26455900-CS345/` is the standalone university GitLab repository and the only
  directory that is version controlled.
- Start at the workspace root for context, but make project changes and run
  project commands, tests, and Git operations against `26455900-CS345/`.
- `agent/`, `.agents/`, `skills-lock.json`, `research/`, `.cursor/`, root
  `AGENTS.md`, and any root `scripts/` are private local resources.
- Reusable Agent Skills live under `.agents/skills/`.
- Official CS345 project specification pointer:
  @agent/specs/cs345-project-specification.md
  (Markdown default; PDF verify-only).
- Work on `main`; do not introduce branches, PRs/MRs, subtree exports,
  publication commits, or repository synchronisation unless explicitly asked.
- Do not stage, commit, pull, push, rewrite history, or modify remotes without
  explicit human authorisation for that Git action.
- Use the detailed rules referenced by `AGENTS.md` when relevant.
- Do not duplicate authoritative policy into new files.
